00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.588
in the county

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:22.455
in South Carolina,

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.090
and that he lived in the scion

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.859
of multiple generations of Murdaugh's

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:26.292
in the legal,

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.328
professional and professional

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.296
and criminal justice system there.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:30.830
At today's

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.831
hearing in the courthouse

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.233
where his grandfather's portrait

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.235
once hung, Murdaugh was sentenced.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.169
He spoke briefly,

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:36.903
but Judge Clifton

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:40.106
Newman had the last word

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.641
I would never,

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.309
under any circumstances, hurt

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.878
my wife, Maggie,

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.980
and I would never under any circumstances

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.481
hurt my son Harper.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.918
It might not have been you.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.254
It might have been

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:57.991
the monster

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.860
you become when you

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:04.330
take 15, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.933
Opioid pills.

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:10.036
Maybe you become another person

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:11.738
Well, tonight, a primetime

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.605
exclusive interview

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.740
with Creighton Waters,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.175
lead prosecutor in the case,

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:16.810
who made it plain in his remarks

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.911
today in court exactly

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:21.481
who Alex Murdaugh was to him.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.783
No one who thought they were close to

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.618
this man knew who he really was.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:27.654
And, Your Honor, that's chilling.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.956
And I've looked in his eyes

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.758
and he liked to stare me down

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.593
because he would walk by me

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.196
during this trial and I could see

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.232
the real Alex Murdaugh

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.900
when he looked at me.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:42.135
Mr.

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:43.803
Waters, thanks for joining us.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:44.370
We just heard

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.406
you say that you knew Alex Murdaugh

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.440
was the killer.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.442
As soon as you looked into his eyes

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.177
when you heard him today

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.513
continuing to declare his innocence,

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.315
I'm wondering what went through your mind

00:01:58.551 --> 00:01:59.953
Nothing more than the same.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.054
I think after he said

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.255
that, I'd got up

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:02.789
and said words

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.289
to the effect

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.291
of what more needs to be said.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:05.592
You know,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.026
the truth is not in this man

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.062
and I think that was a big part

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:09.429
of what

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:13.032
the jury saw and certainly a part of,

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.000
I believe, what

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.602
led them to the right verdict

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.803
that they reached

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:17.804
Were you surprised at all

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:19.839
by the speed of the jury's deliberations?

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.776
Well, I've always said that, you know,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:24.410
trial lawyers

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.712
tend to be a little superstitious.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:26.980
And I try, frankly,

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.182
not to think about things like that.

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.450
And people come up and talk to you

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.284
while you're waiting

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.485
and I'll say this, that

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.220
we had put so much out

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.322
there had been such a huge effort

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.290
by the whole team

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.526
and you saw the whole team in action.

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:40.960
I probably was less

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.662
nervous waiting for this verdict

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.463
than I ever had,

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.031
and not because of overconfidence,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.599
but I just felt like we had done

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.001
all we can do.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.236
But yes, it's usually when you get a

00:02:50.737 --> 00:02:51.538
verdict within a short

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.105
period of time,

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.541
that's generally good for the state.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.408
But, you know,

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.377
you never like to even consider that

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.411
until you actually hear

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:00.046
the word that you want to hear

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.848
this was obviously a very complex trial.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.116
There was a lot of moving parts

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.051
to a lot of evidence was circumstantial.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:05.752
One of the state's

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:06.386
key focuses

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.221
was that the timeline that night

00:03:08.221 --> 00:03:12.091
and when you got up and you went through

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.760
all the things

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.628
that had would have had to have occurred

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.297
to have not been Alex Murdaugh,

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:18.431
I thought that was extraordinary.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:18.898
And I just want to

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:19.933
play that for our viewers.

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:21.601
So what you're

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.802
telling this jury

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.572
is that it's a random vigilante

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.106
that just happened to know

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:27.941
that Paula Maggie

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.543
were both at Moselle on June 7th.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.511
That knew that they would be

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.213
at the kennels alone on June

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.780
the seventh

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.981
and knew that she would not be there,

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.417
but only between the times of eight 49

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:38.551
and nono two,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.620
that they show up without a weapon,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:41.421
assuming that they're going

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:42.755
to find weapons and ammunition

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.691
there, that they commit this crime

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.259
during that short time window.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.060
And then they travel

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.127
the same exact route

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:48.962
that you do

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.631
around the same time to Almeida.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.065
That's what

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.601
you're trying to tell this jury.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.736
You got a lot of factors in there, Mr.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.570
Waters,

00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.806
all of which I do not agree with,

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.008
but some of which I do.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:02.642
It's interesting.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.243
You know, obviously

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.678
that timeline was very crucial evidence.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.179
And,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.715
you know, it really tells a story

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:08.915
you know,

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:09.549
we have to remember,

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:12.752
this guy was a experienced lawyer doing

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.555
sometimes complex accident cases, cases.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:18.725
He's a part time assistant solicitor,

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:19.859
and there's 100 years

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:23.496
of prosecution legacy in his family.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.831
And so as we

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.065
started to look at that timeline,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.533
it really appeared

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:28.868
that this was a man

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:31.204
who was manufacturing an alibi

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.573
and that these time

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.074
periods were more compressed

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.409
than seems reasonable.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:36.576
You know,

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.411
and I think it's kind of ironic

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:41.047
that he was using his cell phone

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:41.881
in this kind of data

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.816
to construct an alibi.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.851
But in the end,

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.752
that kind of video,

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.620
I think, really caught him.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.422
But the chain of circumstances,

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:51.257
even though the burden is on the state,

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.358
the chain of circumstances

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:52.892
that he was trying

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.494
to get this jury to believe,

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:56.863
it just defied any sort of logic

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.098
that this could have occurred.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.800
And I think it was compelling

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:01.401
to the jury.

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.435
Do you have any sense of

00:05:02.435 --> 00:05:02.935
when he

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.338
came up with this decision

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:08.274
to kill his son and to kill his wife?

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.575
Because, as you said,

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.210
he was laying the groundwork

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.547
for this from, you know, that

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:14.847
I mean,

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:15.915
that day, earlier

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:18.051
that day at the very least.

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.052
Do you have any sense of how

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.286
long he had planned this

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.090
You know, one of the things I

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.024
described of him,

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.292
and this is why I think it was important

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:28.361
for the jury to hear this is the

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.696
I think I've used roller coaster

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.630
or hamster wheel

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.398
that he had been on for a decade.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.666
And it's really,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.767
you know, as you look at it

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.368
and look at it

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.904
in its entirety, it's really exhausting.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.907
And these pressures were building.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:43.109
They were coming to a culmination

00:05:43.109 --> 00:05:45.545
and he was running out of options.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.580
I think that

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:48.815
the other thing

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:50.350
that was very important to him

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.352
was this family legacy.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.686
I think that was more important to him

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:54.387
than anything,

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:56.823
aside from his own personal

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:58.624
things that he would suffer

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.593
if all of this was exposed

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:02.528
when that exact moment was I don't know.

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:05.665
But I do know that all these pressures

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:06.132
I called it

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.033
a gathering storm,

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.101
a perfect storm

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.203
were arriving on June 7th.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.771
And whether it was that day

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.039
or whether he'd been thinking about it

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:13.773
for a while,

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:14.774
I don't think we'll ever know.

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:14.941
There's

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.342
only one person who can answer that.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:17.577
But what I do know

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:19.579
is that as those storms

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.247
as that storm arrived,

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:23.015
as he was running out of options,

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.884
as he was faced

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.953
with ruin of not just himself,

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:30.456
but again, that family legacy, as his son

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.592
had become a liability that

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:33.826
threatened to expose him.

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:35.661
That's

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.630
all those came to a head on June 7th,

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.765
and that's the day they died.

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:39.665
You also pointed out

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.268
just sort of the impunity that he

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:44.437
and maybe other members of his family,

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.872
some of his kids, maybe Paul,

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:48.641
but the impunity that he felt he had.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:48.875
I mean,

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:49.475
it was

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:50.176
his great

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:51.811
grandfather, his grandfather,

00:06:51.811 --> 00:06:54.347
his father had all been the prosecutors

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:56.349
in this area in South Carolina.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.618
I mean, it seemed like

00:06:58.618 --> 00:07:01.053
he figured he can do just about anything

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:04.223
Well, absolutely.

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:05.291
And that's what we

00:07:05.291 --> 00:07:07.293
you know, I never knew him.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:10.329
I did work with his father years ago

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:11.597
on a case.

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:13.666
But you know, with with Alex,

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:14.400
as we studied

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:14.934
this more

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.235
and more as the white collar

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:17.437
stuff, as we investigated

00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:18.371
that over months

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:19.939
and months of investigation,

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:20.573
we really started

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.175
to get a picture of this man

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:23.309
in talking to the people

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:24.477
that that knew him

00:07:24.477 --> 00:07:25.278
or thought they knew him,

00:07:25.278 --> 00:07:26.312
because the one thing

00:07:26.312 --> 00:07:27.447
it ultimately revealed

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:28.681
is no matter how close

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.849
the closest people in his life

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:32.018
had no idea who he was,

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.920
which I said was was chilling.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.588
So as we started to discover

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:38.057
that, as we started to realize that,

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:39.358
you know, that became very,

00:07:39.358 --> 00:07:41.194
very clear and very apparent

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:42.728
that he had never faced

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:43.996
accountability in his life

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:46.032
and had always been able to escape that

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:49.235
and that that was more important to him

00:07:49.235 --> 00:07:50.369
than anything.

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:50.803
That's why

00:07:50.803 --> 00:07:51.637
I was always convinced

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.272
that he would testify in this case,

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:54.240
that he was assured

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.043
that he could talk his way out of it

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:57.844
one more time,

00:07:57.844 --> 00:07:59.111
maybe not out of all the trouble,

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:01.247
but certainly talk his way out of this.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:02.715
Obviously, the jury saw otherwise.

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:04.083
He said that even today in the

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:05.785
in the court was

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.220
I would never do anything to hurt

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.422
Maggie or Paul.

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:09.889
Paul, Paul.

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:11.491
He said today,

00:08:11.491 --> 00:08:12.959
which obviously he was talking

00:08:12.959 --> 00:08:15.995
about the murder, but he he was

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:16.329
I mean,

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:18.397
he hurt them repeatedly for

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:20.933
I mean, he was stealing money.

00:08:20.933 --> 00:08:22.535
I mean, he was ruining their lives.

00:08:22.535 --> 00:08:24.003
He was a distant father

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:26.105
because he was a drug addict

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:29.108
who had been lying to everybody.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:29.809
And was stealing

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:30.409
from all of these people.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:31.811
The idea that he hadn't

00:08:31.811 --> 00:08:33.279
already hurt them,

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.815
even without killing them, is

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:36.849
just another lie.

00:08:39.519 --> 00:08:39.819
Yeah.

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.954
And again, I'm not a psychologist

00:08:41.954 --> 00:08:42.555
and I'm not trying

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:43.823
to diagnose anyone here.

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:44.223
But, you know,

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:45.324
I think there's an element

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:46.292
of narcissism there.

00:08:46.292 --> 00:08:50.963
I think that to to some extent,

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:52.298
you know,

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:53.633
he he almost saw this

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:54.767
as a necessary action

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.402
so that they wouldn't

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:57.069
have to suffer

00:08:57.069 --> 00:08:58.204
the consequences

00:08:58.204 --> 00:09:00.840
of of any of this coming out.

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.341
But I think he's very careful

00:09:02.341 --> 00:09:03.910
in how he says things. He's a lawyer.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.211
And his cross-examination

00:09:05.211 --> 00:09:07.513
was very interesting

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:08.347
in dealing with them.

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:09.081
You know, one of the things

00:09:09.081 --> 00:09:10.917
I wanted to do,

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:12.585
unlike a typical cross where you

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:13.653
you really try to control

00:09:13.653 --> 00:09:15.388
the conversation, is to start

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:16.455
with a constructive cross

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:19.258
and get him talking, because I felt like,

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:19.525
you know,

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.027
he believed he could look at that jury

00:09:21.027 --> 00:09:22.595
and really convince them.

00:09:22.595 --> 00:09:23.663
But I felt if I got him

00:09:23.663 --> 00:09:25.197
talking, he would eventually

00:09:26.165 --> 00:09:26.599
you know, he would

00:09:26.599 --> 00:09:27.333
eventually lie

00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:28.434
and they would get to see that

00:09:28.434 --> 00:09:30.002
in real time, see that in action.

00:09:30.002 --> 00:09:30.469
But I think

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:31.637
also they got frustrated

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:32.838
by kind of the things you're saying.

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:33.806
You know, if you really listen to

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.241
what he's saying,

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:36.709
you know, it's very careful

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:38.044
in how he words it.

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:39.645
You know, he says he never hurt them.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:40.212
You know, at one point

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:40.479
he said

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:41.881
and he never, quote, intentionally

00:09:41.881 --> 00:09:42.815
hurt them.

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:43.482
You know, a lot of times

00:09:43.482 --> 00:09:45.651
people try to to,

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:46.319
you know,

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:48.120
live with the things they've done

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:48.754
by, you know,

00:09:48.754 --> 00:09:49.855
qualifying it or say

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:50.823
that wasn't the real money

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:51.891
or things like that.

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:54.260
He had a very well known in common

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.329
tell that whether it was on the videos

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:57.763
of the law enforcement interviews

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:59.198
or even on the stand,

00:09:59.198 --> 00:10:00.833
that when he said things that are a lie,

00:10:00.833 --> 00:10:02.935
he would shake his head forward like this

00:10:02.935 --> 00:10:04.337
while he's doing that.

00:10:04.337 --> 00:10:04.804
Is that right?

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:06.072
These were all things that some

00:10:06.072 --> 00:10:07.573
grand jury of course. Yeah.

00:10:08.541 --> 00:10:08.808
Yeah.

00:10:08.808 --> 00:10:09.575
And so,

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:09.842
you know, and

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:11.010
I pointed that out to the jury,

00:10:11.010 --> 00:10:13.145
but I think the main thing was,

00:10:13.145 --> 00:10:13.779
you know,

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:15.348
establishing with them

00:10:15.348 --> 00:10:17.083
that nobody who knew this man

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:18.351
knew who he really was.

00:10:18.351 --> 00:10:19.652
He lies effortlessly.

00:10:19.652 --> 00:10:21.787
He lies convincingly.

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:22.955
And he looked in their eyes

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.890
and lied to them about

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.626
perhaps the most important fact

00:10:26.626 --> 00:10:28.794
of this whole case,

00:10:28.794 --> 00:10:29.462
you know, about

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:32.298
when is the last time he saw

00:10:32.298 --> 00:10:34.500
his wife and his son alive

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:36.302
and only when he was back into yet

00:10:36.302 --> 00:10:36.902
another corner

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:39.338
did he come up with this latest version.

00:10:39.338 --> 00:10:42.508
And obviously, the jury saw through that.

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:43.576
And I think,

00:10:43.576 --> 00:10:44.810
you know, he got up there very,

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:46.712
very confident that he was going to

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:48.180
you know, this is his community

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.415
and he's always been able to do this,

00:10:49.415 --> 00:10:50.216
that he was going to,

00:10:50.216 --> 00:10:51.550
you know, get them on his side.

